6. CRITICAL ADDITION — IDEMPOTENCY AND DUPLICATE PREVENTION

Every integration request and every per-record operation must have a stable
unique identifier and durable processing record. Design for at-least-once job
delivery without creating duplicate SAP items.

Required controls:
- Unique request and record-operation identifiers.
- Unique constraints for the relevant idempotency keys.
- Explicit global-item-to-SAP identity mappings.
- Concurrency-safe claim/lock of records.
- Safe handling of duplicate dispatch and user double-click.
- Safe recovery after worker restart.
- Distinguish not-started, in-progress, succeeded, failed, and outcome-unknown.
- Reconcile the target before retrying an outcome-unknown write.
- Never retry a permanent validation or authorization error indefinitely.
- Preserve successful per-record outcomes when a batch partially fails.
- Do not claim exactly-once delivery unless the actual implementation can
  guarantee it; document the implemented delivery semantics.

7. CRITICAL ADDITION — GLOBAL ITEM IDENTITY REGISTRY

Maintain a permanent global item identifier that is independent of SAP ItemCode.
Map it explicitly to each SAP company/database and its SAP ItemCode or returned
business-object identity.

Support:
- One global item mapped to one or more authorized SAP companies when policy
  requires multi-company distribution.
- Company-specific mapping status and synchronization history.
- Duplicate and conflicting mapping detection.
- Disabled, retired, and historical mappings without deleting audit history.
- Explicit handling when an SAP item exists but no portal mapping is present.
- Explicit handling when the portal item exists but the SAP mapping is missing.
- Policy-driven resolution of code conflicts; never guess silently.

Do not assume that the same ItemCode is valid or identical across every SAP
company. Do not silently change an existing item's permanent identity when item
code-generation rules are modified.

8. CRITICAL ADDITION — RECONCILIATION AND SYNCHRONIZATION STATUS

Implement scheduled and on-demand reconciliation between portal records and SAP
results using supported SAP interfaces. Detect:
- Approved portal items never submitted.
- Requests submitted but with unknown outcomes.
- SAP items created without a confirmed portal mapping.
- Portal mappings whose SAP item cannot be found.
- Stale or inconsistent synchronization status.
- Conflicting field values according to the defined field ownership policy.
- Duplicate candidates and invalid identity mappings.
- Records stuck in processing beyond a configured threshold.

Display clear status and recommended actions. Do not automatically overwrite
conflicting business data. Require authorized review for conflicts that cannot
be resolved deterministically. Record reconciliation runs, findings, decisions,
