ADDITIONAL UI / FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS — GLOBAL ITEM MASTER
SEARCH, SORT, FILTER, PAGINATION AND BULK IMPORT REPAIR
====================================================================

PURPOSE

Apply the following corrections and enhancements to the existing Global Item Master page. These requirements are additive to the complete existing master prompt. Preserve the existing Global Item Master data model, Item Code and Description rule engine, classification masters, approval/governance workflow, SAP Business One integration, role permissions, audit trail and all other previously specified functionality.

1. PAGE AND ACTION LABEL CHANGES

1.1 Rename the navigation/page label:
- Existing label: “Global Item Master & Import / Export”
- Required label: “Global Item Master”

The bulk import and export features must remain available inside the Global Item Master page through clearly named actions, tabs, toolbar options or a dedicated import/export dialog. Removing “Import / Export” from the page title must not remove either capability.

1.2 Rename the item creation action:
- Existing label: “Create Item (Maker)”
- Required label: “Create Item”

Update all relevant buttons, headings, breadcrumbs, accessible labels, tooltips, page titles and user-facing references consistently. Do not rename internal API routes, database entities or identifiers unless required by the existing architecture and handled through a safe migration. This is a user-facing label change.

1.3 Preserve role-based access:
- Users who are authorized to view items must continue to see the item list.
- Only users with the required permission may create, edit, import, export, approve, activate or perform SAP-related actions.
- Hiding a button is not sufficient security; enforce permissions on backend APIs.

2. GLOBAL ITEM MASTER LIST — REQUIRED COLUMNS

The Global Item Master list must show the following columns, subject to the user's permissions and the actual schema:
1. Global Item Code.
2. Category.
3. Generated Description.
4. Branch Availability.
5. Governance Status.
6. SAP Status.
7. Action.

Column behavior:
- Global Item Code: show the permanent global identifier, with a copy action only if permitted.
- Category: show the configured category label/code.
- Generated Description: show the generated description from the applicable approved rule version; use safe truncation with a way to inspect the full description.
- Branch Availability: show authorized branch/site availability in a readable form, such as branch names or a count with detail view. Do not invent availability where no verified record exists.
- Governance Status: show the actual workflow status, such as Draft, Pending Approval, Approved, Rejected, Retired or the statuses supported by the existing workflow. Use the actual configured status model rather than hardcoding a contradictory set.
- SAP Status: show the actual SAP integration state, such as Not Synced, Pending, In Progress, Synced, Failed or other states defined by the current integration model. Do not label a record Synced unless a verified SAP response/reconciliation supports that status.
- Action: display only the actions authorized for the current user and valid for the row's current state, for example View, Edit Draft, Submit, Approve/Reject, View SAP Details, Retry Synchronization or History. Use the actual application's permissions and state transitions.

If the actual database or existing page uses different internal field names, map the required display columns to verified fields. Do not create duplicate or fabricated data solely to populate a column. If Branch Availability is not yet represented in the schema, report the gap and propose a reviewed data-model/API change before displaying a fake value.

3. SEARCH — REQUIRED BEHAVIOR

Implement a functional server-backed search field for the Global Item Master list.

Search should support the relevant fields available in the approved schema, including:
- Global Item Code.
- Category code/name.
- Generated Description.
- Branch/site name or identifier, where authorized and available.
- Governance Status.
- SAP Status.

Requirements:
- Search must work with partial values and reasonable case-insensitive matching where appropriate.
- Define how whitespace and code normalization are handled.
- Search must combine correctly with active filters and sort order.
- Search must be enforced by the backend query, not only by filtering the rows currently loaded in the browser.
- Debounce interactive search requests where appropriate without losing the user's latest query.
- Provide a clear-search control and a useful empty-result state.
- Preserve search and filter values while the user moves between pages or opens and returns from an item detail page, where appropriate.
- Do not search fields the user is not authorized to access.
- Use parameterized queries/ORM filters; never concatenate user search text into raw SQL.
- Apply pagination and limits to protect performance.

4. SORTING — REQUIRED BEHAVIOR

Provide sortable headers for relevant columns:
- Global Item Code.
- Category.
- Generated Description.
- Branch Availability, only if there is a defined sortable value.
- Governance Status.
- SAP Status.
- Created/updated date if included in the visible column set or advanced filters.

Requirements:
- Support ascending and descending order.
- Show the active sort column and direction clearly.
- Sorting must apply to the full result set on the server, not just the current page.
- Use a deterministic secondary sort key, such as a stable item ID or Global Item Code, so records do not jump unpredictably when values are equal.
- Whitelist sortable fields in the backend. Never pass arbitrary user-supplied column names directly into SQL.
- Sorting must combine correctly with search, filters and pagination.
- For derived columns such as Branch Availability, define a valid query/aggregate sort method before enabling the sort control. If no reliable sort is defined, do not display a misleading sortable affordance.

5. FILTERS — REQUIRED BEHAVIOR

Provide a filter panel or toolbar with filters for:
- Category.
- Branch Availability / Branch.
- Governance Status.
- SAP Status.

Also support useful additional filters where the underlying schema supports them:
- Created date range.
- Updated date range.
- Created by.
- Item Code prefix or exact code.
- Items with/without branch assignments.
- SAP integration failure/pending status.
- Retired/inactive items, subject to permission.
- Classification values, where they are useful and the schema supports efficient filtering.

Filter requirements:
- Filters must be backed by real values from the authorized database records or approved master data.
- Support multiple simultaneous filters.
- Show active filters as removable chips or equivalent indicators.
- Provide Clear All Filters.
- Preserve active filters while navigating pages.
- Filter options must respect authorization and any branch/company scope.
- Define and implement correct behavior when filters are combined with search and sort.
- Show the number of matching records if it can be obtained accurately and efficiently.
- If a filter is not supported by existing data, identify the schema gap rather than fabricate filter values.

6. MULTIPLE-PAGE SUPPORT / SERVER-SIDE PAGINATION

The Global Item Master must support multiple pages of records. Do not load every item into the browser merely to implement the list.

Provide:
- Page navigation: Previous, Next, first/last where practical.
- Current page and total pages when a reliable count is available.
- Total matching record count, where supported.
- Configurable page size, with reasonable options such as 10, 25, 50 and 100 records per page.
- A visible range indicator, for example “Showing 26–50 of 427”.
- Disabled states for Previous/Next at boundaries.
- Stable ordering to prevent duplicates or missing rows when navigating.
- Server-side pagination applied after authorization, search, filters and sorting.
- A safe maximum page size.
- Appropriate empty state for no matching records.
- Loading and error states.
- Keyboard accessibility and responsive behavior.

For large or frequently changing datasets, use a reliable pagination strategy. Offset pagination is acceptable if performance and consistency are adequate; consider cursor/keyset pagination if required by actual scale. The UI must not claim an exact total count unless the backend returns a correct count. When records change during navigation, use deterministic sorting and document the behavior.

When search/filter/sort changes, reset to the appropriate first page so the user is not left on a now-invalid page. When the user changes page size, apply the defined behavior consistently.

7. BULK IMPORT — CURRENTLY NOT WORKING; MUST BE DIAGNOSED AND FIXED

The existing Bulk Import feature is reported as not working. Treat this as a defect requiring investigation and repair, not as a request to add only a visual button.

First inspect the current implementation end-to-end:
- Frontend import entry point and file selector.
- Accepted file types and size limits.
- Upload request and multipart/form-data handling.
- API route and authentication.
- Backend parsing/validation.
- Column/header mapping.
- Classification code/value resolution.
- Item Code and Item Description rule resolution.
- Database writes and transaction boundaries.
- Duplicate detection.
- Validation error reporting.
- Approval/governance behavior.
- Import job state and progress reporting.
- Audit records.
- Error logs and browser/network/server responses.
- Existing test cases and current observed failure.

Identify the actual root cause before modifying code. Do not assume the failure is caused by any particular component without evidence. Produce a concise defect diagnosis that records the observed failure, root cause, affected files/components, correction and tests.

7.1 Import entry point and supported formats
- Keep Bulk Import accessible from the Global Item Master page.
- Clearly state supported file formats, for example CSV and XLSX only if the actual implementation supports them.
- Provide a downloadable template generated from the current approved import schema.
