    deleting data or affecting ItemMaster.
15. Re-enabling BPMaster restores the module according to saved configuration and
    current user permissions.
16. Module Builder can define a sample future module using metadata and permissions
    without weakening security or bypassing approval.
17. Audit records show who created/edited/approved/verified/synchronized a BP and
    when, with correlation IDs and sanitized errors.
18. Run unit tests, API/integration tests, UI tests, migration checks, and target
    environment smoke tests. Clearly label tests that could not run because SAP or
    a verification provider was unavailable.

DELIVERY EXPECTATIONS
Implement this as an addition to the current application, not a replacement. First
inspect the existing code, routes, schema, navigation, module registry, role model,
SAP integration, and available source document. Produce a gap analysis and field
mapping register. Then implement the BPMaster pages and backend behavior in small,
reviewable increments, reusing existing components and styles. Keep the existing
ItemMaster working. Show actual changed files and test results where available.
Do not fabricate screenshots, API responses, SAP identifiers, GST verification
results, or passing test results. Do not claim production readiness until the
acceptance tests have been run in the intended environment.
